
    <div class="card">
      <strong>Short version:</strong> The Guitar Workbench is offline-first.
      Your scores, recordings, and creative content stay on your device.
      Optional anonymous Firebase Analytics helps improve the product and can be
      turned off in Settings. We do not sell your data and we do not show ads.
    </div>
    <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      This Privacy Policy explains how <strong>Francisco Pampulha</strong>
      (“we”, “us”, “the developer”) handles information in connection with
      <strong>The Guitar Workbench</strong> (the “App”).
    </p>
    <p>
      Contact for privacy questions:
      <a href="mailto:franciscopampulha@gmail.com">franciscopampulha@gmail.com</a>
    </p>
    <h2>2. Scope</h2>
    <p>
      This policy covers the Android and iOS versions of The Guitar Workbench.
      It does not cover third-party websites, stores (Google Play / Apple App Store),
      or other apps, which have their own policies.
    </p>
    <h2>3. No account and no cloud sync</h2>
    <p>
      The App does not require an account, login, or cloud sync. There is no
      developer-operated backend that stores your songs, tabs, or practice files.
      Creative content you create or import remains under your control on your device
      (and on any location you choose if you export or share files yourself).
    </p>
    <h2>4. Information processed on your device</h2>
    <p>Depending on how you use the App, it may store locally on your device:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Scores, tabs, library indexes, backups, and related creative files</li>
      <li>Instrument profiles, settings, preferences, and practice history</li>
      <li>Optional audio memos / recordings you choose to capture</li>
      <li>Temporary audio used for features such as tuner, transcription, play-along scoring, and similar tools</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      This on-device information is not uploaded to our servers for storage.
      If you use the operating system’s share sheet or export features, you choose
      where those files go.
    </p>
    <h2>5. Microphone</h2>
    <p>
      The App may request microphone permission for features such as tuning,
      transcription, chord listening, play-along / runner scoring, and audio memos.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Microphone audio for these features is processed <strong>on your device</strong>.</li>
      <li>We do not use microphone audio to build advertising profiles.</li>
      <li>We do not upload your performances, transcriptions, or memo contents to Firebase Analytics.</li>
      <li>You can deny microphone access in system settings; related features will not work until permission is granted.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>6. Analytics (optional)</h2>
    <p>
      Unless you opt out, the App uses <strong>Google Firebase Analytics</strong>
      (with Google Analytics / GA4) to understand aggregated product usage and improve the App.
    </p>
    <p>Analytics is designed to be privacy-bounded:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Collection starts only after the App can apply your saved preference.</li>
      <li>You can turn analytics off at any time in <strong>Settings → Anonymous usage analytics</strong>.</li>
      <li>We do <strong>not</strong> send score IDs or titles, repertoire content, recordings, transcription output, notes, free text, profile names, file paths, or other creative content to Analytics.</li>
      <li>Allowed signals are limited to product taxonomy such as screen/route names, tool names, onboarding goals, and similar non-creative action types.</li>
      <li>Advertising storage, advertising personalization, and Android advertising-ID collection for this App remain disabled.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Google may process analytics data as an independent controller or processor
      according to Google’s terms and privacy documentation for Firebase / Google Analytics.
      See Google’s privacy resources for Firebase and Google Analytics for details on
      their processing, retention, and international transfers.
    </p>
    <h2>7. Crash and diagnostics data</h2>
    <p>
      Your device platform or store (for example Google Play / Apple) may collect
      crash or diagnostic information according to your device settings and the
      store’s policies. Separately, if we later enable optional crash-reporting SDKs,
      we will update this policy before doing so.
    </p>
    <h2>8. Purchases</h2>
    <p>
      The current release is free and does not offer in-app purchases.
      If paid features are added later, billing will be handled by Google Play or
      the App Store; we will update this policy and store disclosures accordingly.
    </p>
    <h2>9. Advertising and data sale</h2>
    <p>
      The App does not display third-party advertising.
      We do not sell your personal information.
      We do not share creative content with data brokers.
    </p>
    <h2>10. Children</h2>
    <p>
      The App is a general music-practice tool and is not directed at children
      under 13 (or the equivalent minimum age in your country). We do not knowingly
      collect personal information from children. If you believe a child has provided
      personal information through Analytics despite our design limits, contact us and
      we will take appropriate steps.
    </p>
    <h2>11. Retention</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>On-device content:</strong> retained until you delete it or uninstall the App (subject to any device backups you control).</li>
      <li><strong>Analytics:</strong> retained according to our Firebase / Google Analytics configuration and Google’s retention controls; opting out stops further Analytics collection from the App on that device.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>12. International users and legal bases (EEA/UK)</h2>
    <p>
      If you are in the European Economic Area or UK, we process Analytics data based on
      <strong>legitimate interests</strong> in understanding and improving the App,
      and/or your choice to keep analytics enabled. You can object by disabling analytics
      in Settings. On-device processing needed to provide features you request is based on
      <strong>performance of the contract / requested service</strong> and your device permissions.
    </p>
    <h2>13. Your choices and rights</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Disable analytics in App Settings</li>
      <li>Revoke microphone (and other) permissions in system settings</li>
      <li>Delete local App data by clearing app storage or uninstalling</li>
      <li>Export or delete creative files you control on the device</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Depending on your location, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, or
      restrict certain personal data, or to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority.
      For Analytics data held by Google, you may also need to use Google’s tools or contact us
      so we can help where we can.
    </p>
    <h2>14. Data security</h2>
    <p>
      We design the App so creative content does not need to leave your device for core features.
      No method of electronic storage or transmission is perfectly secure; protect your device
      with a passcode/biometrics and be careful when exporting or sharing files.
    </p>
    <h2>15. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this Privacy Policy when the App’s data practices change.
      The “Last updated” date at the top will change when we do. Continued use of the App
      after an update means you acknowledge the revised policy.
    </p>
